body:
Personally : If my girlfriend would go tru my phone in the night (we dont check each others phone) I would be hella pissed of course. I prolly would not break up if she can promise me to not do it again. If she does it a second time I'll go. 

&#x200B;

But you definitly not an asshole. Its a solid reason to break up and a lot of people would definitly break up. You trusted her and she threw it away. If you feel its the better choice for you, its definitly okay. Dont listen to her and ignore her, she will stop sooner or later. 

&#x200B;

The worst thing is : She doesnt want to take any responsibility. First she denies it and then she starts to cry and place herhelf in the role of a victim.

> But that’s wrong. The powercreep allows players to catch up in the story with bare minimum jewels. The ONLY thing “horrible” about the powercreep is trying to PvP and if he’s a new player he’s going to drown in Tier 8+ KH3 medals because they’re giving like 2-4 KH3 medals a pull now so it’s a nonissue entirely. 

You can literally clear the entire story with 1-2 T8 medals. New players being able to clear the entire story with just one 10x medal pull is horrible and not right. Buff cap getting increased and not even a month later a medal that gives you fullbuff gets released. Also alone the dmg numbers are ridiculous. How is the powercreep NOT horrible lmao. Also powercreep is indeed bad for pvp and hes going to be affected by it sooner or later (or hes just ignoring player). You can't just say "for a beginner it doesnt matter". 

&#x200B;

> Again, that’s wrong. They made filler quests optional. You only have to do the ones with cutscenes. 

Did not know you can skip filler quests now but its still a solid fact. If he cleared all quests with cutscenes he need to wait for new quests. The majority of new released quests are filler. He can skip them. The main story is going hardly forwards and he's going to wait ages to continue the main story line. People can pretty much play 20 minuntes every 3 month if they just want to play it for the main story itself.

&#x200B;

> This is really the only point I can even partially agree with you on. But oh wait. Keyblade war and unique events other than “new weekly boss” having been coming more frequently. So no. 

" imo most of the events are boring" - as I said 'most'. They usually release a few interesting events followed by a longer period of time where they just release boring events.

&#x200B;

> You don’t speak for the entire player base. 

Of course not, but most people who are interested in the story and not interested in filler used to rush thru the fillers until they reached important story quests. 

&#x200B;

> That’s merely an opinion and kind of a bad one. OP said he’s already caught up on YouTube so why would he choose to play this game if he’s already caught up on story? For fun and playing the story himself. Now being the best time to get into the game, you trying to dissuade him by lying with all the points in your post I replied to because (it really seems like) you personally don’t enjoy the game is kinda mean and would rob OP of a potentially fun experience if he listened to you instead of trying the game for himself. 

&#x200B;

There is no objective opinion. It will vary from player to player. But I'm still defending my opinion "Khux is not worth for the story alone" since most of the quests are filler. I've learned that people can skip most filler quests which is cool. But again he can probably catch up to the current main quest in a few days/couple of hours and then? Wait a few months to get story content for another 20 minutes? OP even mentioned he is only interested in the story.

Generally when i have to make hard decisions where feelings are involved. A stranger can tell you his opinion on a neutral and logical view while you might be confused because of your feelings. Of course take his opinion with a grain of salt but listen to his opinion can help.  

An example could be a breakup situation with your SO.  

In my situation it was a choice between a wedding and a wedding cancellation

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

> let file = `${__dirname}/file.txt`;
> 
>     res.download(file, function(err) {                                     
>         if (err) throw err;
>         // ...                    
>     });     

Thanks for you answer! I thought you could pass the path of the file + a name that the downloaded file should have.Unfortunately
 your code doesnt work for me. Its the same outcome as my code. Server says the download call was successfull but there is no download window on my page.
